          "question": {
            "text": "How will raise in temperature affects the viscosity of liquids and gases?",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "7kdb5",
              "text": "\r\nBoth increases\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "akKfT",
              "text": "\r\nBoth decreases\r\n",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "PPUF7",
              "text": "\r\nIn case of liquids, decreases and in case of gases, increases.\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "EqHC5",
              "text": "\r\nIn case of liquid, increases and in case of gases, decreases.",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "In case of liquids, cohesive forces decrease and hence, their viscosity decreases while increasing the temperature.\r\nHowever, in case of gases, with the increase in temperature kinetic energy of gaseous molecules increases and the molecules become more mobile.",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
